## Important Details
- Working directory: `/home/runner/work/rbops/rbops/redblue`; only read/write inside it. Scratch space must be `./target/tmp/`.
- Do NOT touch `.github/workflows/`, `rbops/`, `.opencode/agent/`, or `rbops/phases.json`.
- Never weaken/delete/skip tests or suppressions; no new `#[ignore]`, `// skip`, `allow(clippy::`.
- `Value` variants are fixed: `Nothing/Number/Text/YesNo/List/Record/Object/Function/Builtin` (+ `Date`, `Duration`). Do not add variants.
- `.rb` extension, `to … end`, `set x to`, `say`, trailing commas/interpolation, existing tests/examples/modules are invariants.
- `src/stdlib.rs` has `MODULES`, `ALIAS_MODULES`, `MODULE_MEMBERS`, `builtins()`, `BUILTIN_NAMES`, `BUILTIN_SIGNATURES`; both engines resolve builtins through shared `runtime::builtin` then `stdlib::builtin`.
- `src/runtime.rs` `pub fn builtin(span, name, args) -> Result<Option<Value>>` is the fallible shared dispatcher; `stdlib::builtin_function` handles infallible flat builtins.
- `property` handles `Record` (missing field → `nothing`), `Date`, `Duration`; does NOT handle `Value::Object`.
- `list.shift` returns the first element and does NOT remove it; `skip(xs, 1)` is the quadratic front-removal equivalent.
- Docs tests reconcile `SPEC.md` and `README.md` standard-library sections against `MODULES`/`MODULE_MEMBERS`; adding `collections` required doc entries in both.
- `tests/stdlib_module_docs_test.rs` requires every registered builtin to have a row in `answerable_builtins` or `known_gaps`.
- `tests/stdlib_module_names_test.rs` requires a row for each documented module in `every_module_the_documents_name_answers_a_call`.
- Final API implemented:
  - `collections.counter(items)` → record `{counts: [[key,count],…], missing: 0}`
  - `collections.count(counter, key)` → count or `0`
  - `collections.most_common(counter)` → list of `[key,count]`, count desc, stable first-appearance ties
  - `collections.defaultdict(factory)` → record `{entries: [[key,value],…], factory: value}`
  - `collections.get(dict, key)` → record `{value, dict}`; creates entry on first read using factory value
  - `collections.put(dict, key, value)` → updated dict (`set` is a keyword, so `put` replaced it)
  - `collections.deque([items])` → linked-node deque record `{front, back}`
  - `collections.push_left/push_right(dq, v)` → updated deque
  - `collections.pop_left/pop_right(dq)` → record `{value, deque}`, empty → `nothing`
  - `collections.namedtuple(names, values)` → record with named fields; validates lengths/duplicates/text names
  - `collections.field(record, name)` → value or catchable runtime error naming missing field
- Deque uses linked records `{value, next}` for `front`/`back` to avoid O(n) `Arc::make_mut` copies on each push; reversal on empty side gives amortized O(1).
- Defaultdict factory is a documented **value**, not callable. This is explicit in docs because native builtins cannot synchronously call Redblue functions without risky VM changes.
- Counter reuses `group_value_hash` for O(n) mixed-key grouping.
- Measured costs (debug build, isolated list literals):
  - N=4000: `shift` 0.0285s, `skip(xs,1)` 0.2800s, deque `pop_left` 0.0843s
  - N=8000: `shift` 0.0517s, `skip(xs,1)` 1.0648s, deque `pop_left` 0.1669s
  - `shift` scales linearly (~1.8x for 2x N) and never removes; `skip` scales ~3.8x and is quadratic. Deque scales ~2x.
  - Build+drain N=4000: deque 0.1198s vs skip 0.7119s; N=8000: deque 0.2324s vs skip 2.7278s.
- `cargo test --all-targets` is ~15 min / 67 binaries; iterate with targeted `cargo test <name>` only.
- Four gates: `cargo fmt --all -- --check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo test --all-targets`, `../rbops/verify.sh "phase-099"`.
- `REPORT.md` must be `phases/phase-099/REPORT.md` with exact AGENTS.md section 4 tables and measured `list.shift` cost.
- `tests/report_markdown_test.rs` requires headings: `## What changed`, `## Tests added`, `## Gates`, plus likely `## Invariants touched`.

